---
/**
 * How Claude gets in: the chat in the app or Claude Code over MCP, both through the same tools,
 * and the architecture in one picture: clients on top, the engine below, your Mac underneath.
 */
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
import { LINKS, MCP_ADD, TOOL_COUNT } from "../lib/site";
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";

const ways = [
  {
    title: "In the app",
    text: "Open the Agent tab, paste your own Anthropic API key, and talk: type, or hold a key and speak. The key stays on your Mac.",
  },
  {
    title: "From Claude Code",
    text: "GrooveKit ships an MCP server, the standard way Claude picks up tools. Register it once and Claude Code works on the project your window has open.",
    code: MCP_ADD,
  },
];

const steps = [
  ["Reads before it touches", "The song, your notes, the style’s guide and maps. Then it searches your library and auditions candidates in the song."],
  ["Changes the song in one step", "A request becomes typed commands applied atomically. Each lands in your window as it happens, outlined in violet."],
  ["Checks its own work", "It renders and measures: loudness, spectrum, masking, the fit against the references. Adjusts, renders again."],
  ["Asks when it’s your call", "When a sound is a matter of taste, it offers A, B, C to pick by ear, and remembers what you chose."],
];
---

<section id="agent" class="scroll-mt-16 border-t border-line py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="container-site">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,0.8fr)] lg:items-end">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The agent</p>
        <h2 class="title mt-4">Claude, with the whole studio in its hands.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-dim">
        {TOOL_COUNT} tools over the{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.mcp} class="text-fg underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-fg">Model Context Protocol</a>,
        built on the same engine API as the interface. Anything you can click, the agent can do;
        anything it does, you can see, change and undo.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
      {ways.map((w) => (
        <article class="rounded-2xl bg-panel p-6 ring-1 ring-line sm:p-7">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.015em]">{w.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-dim">{w.text}</p>
          {w.code && (
            <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-bg px-3.5 py-3 text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-fg ring-1 ring-line"><code><span class="text-faint select-none">$ </span>{w.code}</code></pre>
          )}
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <dl class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {steps.map(([t, d], i) => (
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-panel p-6 ring-1 ring-line">
          <dt class="flex items-baseline gap-3 font-semibold">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">0{i + 1}</span>
            {t}
          </dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-dim">{d}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <!-- Architecture -->
    <div class="mt-20 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.8fr)_minmax(0,1.2fr)] lg:gap-14">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.1rem)] leading-[1.1] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance">One engine. Two kinds of client.</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-dim">
          The engine is a C++ audio process that owns the project: it plays, records, renders,
          hosts plugins and keeps the history. It speaks JSON-RPC over a local WebSocket:
          commands in, live patches out. The app’s window is one client; the MCP server, which
          turns {TOOL_COUNT} tools into those commands, is another. Both see the same song at the
          same time, which is why the agent’s edits appear in your window as it makes them.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-dim">
          Listening, the models that hear samples and reference tracks, runs on your Mac. Only
          the chat leaves it, to Anthropic with your key, or to Claude Code’s provider.
        </p>
        <a href={`${base}docs/`} class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-accent underline-offset-4 hover:underline">
          Read the docs <Icon name="arrow" class="size-3.5" />
        </a>
      </div>

      <figure class="min-w-0" aria-label="Architecture: the app window and Claude (in the app or in Claude Code, through the MCP server) are clients of one engine, which owns the project folder and talks to your plugins, samples and audio hardware.">
        <div class="gk-arch rounded-2xl bg-panel p-5 ring-1 ring-line sm:p-7" aria-hidden="true">
          <!-- Clients -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
            <div class="gk-arch-box">
              <span class="gk-arch-kicker">You</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-name">The app</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-sub">React UI, Tauri</span>
            </div>
            <div class="gk-arch-box gk-arch-agent">
              <span class="gk-arch-kicker">Claude</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-name">Chat in the app</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-sub">your API key</span>
            </div>
            <div class="gk-arch-box gk-arch-agent">
              <span class="gk-arch-kicker">Claude</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-name">Claude Code</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-sub">or any MCP client</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <!-- Connectors to the MCP server -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
            <div class="gk-arch-line"></div>
            <div class="gk-arch-line"></div>
            <div class="gk-arch-line"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
            <div class="gk-arch-line h-auto self-stretch"></div>
            <div class="gk-arch-box gk-arch-agent col-span-2">
              <span class="gk-arch-kicker">MCP server</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-name">{TOOL_COUNT} tools</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-sub">search, edit, render, measure, listen, master…</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
            <div class="gk-arch-line"></div>
            <div class="gk-arch-line col-span-2"></div>
          </div>
          <!-- Engine -->
          <div class="gk-arch-bus">JSON-RPC over a local WebSocket · commands in, live patches out</div>
          <div class="gk-arch-box gk-arch-engine mt-3">
            <span class="gk-arch-kicker">Engine</span>
            <span class="gk-arch-name">C++ · JUCE · Tracktion Engine</span>
            <span class="gk-arch-sub">plays, records, renders, hosts plugins, keeps the history, hears samples and references</span>
          </div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
            <div class="gk-arch-line"></div>
            <div class="gk-arch-line"></div>
            <div class="gk-arch-line"></div>
          </div>
          <!-- Your Mac -->
          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
            <div class="gk-arch-box gk-arch-mac">
              <span class="gk-arch-name">Project folder</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-sub">song.json, history, takes</span>
            </div>
            <div class="gk-arch-box gk-arch-mac">
              <span class="gk-arch-name">Samples &amp; plugins</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-sub">your library, VST3, AU</span>
            </div>
            <div class="gk-arch-box gk-arch-mac">
              <span class="gk-arch-name">Audio &amp; MIDI</span>
              <span class="gk-arch-sub">speakers, interface, hardware</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
